{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Upon a bare mountain.</b> Some say it is from the root נשף (Isaiah 5:11), like שחרות. The correct view is that it is from the root שפי'ם (1 Kings 18), and the nun is for the nifal binyan, and its meaning is high, or it has no root cognate:" "<b>For them.</b> For those who come against Babylon to fight against it:" "<b>And they shall enter.</b> And immediately they shall come and enter the city, for they will seize it:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Resolved מ\"ק י\"ח as 1 Kings 18 based on the root שפים appearing in that chapter (v. 42); standard chapter-verse abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:33.218803252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}